From: Ilya I. Nikitin <ilya.i.nikitin@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] aaa: measure white balance before preview color processing

The preview is gamma-encoded, color-matrix transformed and clipped. Dividing
its channel averages by previous gains does not recover sensor RGB and
creates an unstable magenta/green feedback loop on both Blade S6 cameras.

Measure Bayer white balance in a linear shader pass before gains, DCP and
gamma. Reject near-black and saturated samples, retain gains when no valid
samples exist, and keep preview statistics for exposure and focus. Reuse
the readback buffer and run the extra pass only on existing AAA frames.
Keep the YUV path unchanged.

--- a/data/debayer.frag
+++ b/data/debayer.frag
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 uniform mat3 color_matrix;
 uniform float inv_gamma;
 uniform float blacklevel;
+uniform bool statistics;
 
 varying vec2 top_left_uv;
 varying vec2 top_right_uv;
@@ -34,6 +35,10 @@
     #endif
 
     color -= blacklevel;
+    if (statistics) {
+        gl_FragColor = vec4(max(color, vec3(0.0)), 1);
+        return;
+    }
     color = color_matrix * color;
 
     vec3 gamma_color = pow(max(color, vec3(0.0)), vec3(inv_gamma));
